narrative:
## Building a Task Manager

A todo list needs three operations: add a task, complete a task (remove it), and show what's left.

### Storing Tasks

```xiom
let todos: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
```

Each task is a string. We'll push new tasks onto the end.

### Adding a Task

```xiom
fn add_task(todos: Vec[Str], task: Str) {
  todos.push(task);
}
```

### Completing a Task

We need to remove a task by its number. Since Vecs don't have `.remove(index)`, we build the logic:

```xiom
fn complete_task(todos: Vec[Str], index: Int) -> Option[Str] {
  match todos.get(index) {
    Some(task) -> {
      let removed = task;
      let new_todos: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
      let i: Int = 0;
      while i < todos.len() {
        if i != index {
          match todos.get(i) {
            Some(t) -> new_todos.push(t);
            None -> {}
          }
        }
        i = i + 1;
      }
      return Some(removed);
    }
    None -> None
  }
}
```

### Listing All Tasks

```xiom
fn list_tasks(todos: Vec[Str]) {
  let i: Int = 0;
  while i < todos.len() {
    match todos.get(i) {
      Some(task) -> io.println(string.int_to_str(i + 1) + ". " + task);
      None -> {}
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
}
```

### Full Program

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let todos: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  todos.push("Submit report");
  todos.push("Buy groceries");
  todos.push("Call dentist");

  io.println("My Todos:");
  list_tasks(todos);
  io.println("Remaining: " + string.int_to_str(todos.len()));
  return 0;
}
```

